PREAMBLE

Zeta Lite is a WebAssembly build of the Zeta database engine, intended to run
in a web browser (or a WASI host). It is free to use — including for
commercial purposes — at no charge. It is not open source: the engine source
code is not included in this distribution, and a few narrow restrictions apply
(see RESTRICTIONS below).

This license covers the compiled Zeta Lite artifact and the hand-authored
materials distributed with it. The engine source code lives in a separate,
closed repository and is available only to parties under a separate
Non-Disclosure Agreement and arrangement; nothing here grants access to that
source.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ACCEPTANCE

By downloading, installing, running, or redistributing the compiled Zeta Lite
artifact (the `.wasm` file and its accompanying JavaScript/TypeScript glue,
collectively the "Software"), you agree to be bound by the terms of this
license. If you do not agree, do not use the Software.

